      "tag": "Both",
      "h2": "Bitte does double duty",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Bitte</strong> means both <strong>please</strong> AND <strong>you're welcome</strong>. Context tells you which. If you say 'Danke' to a German they often reply 'Bitte'.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Thanks",
      "h2": "Saying Thanks",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Danke</strong> = thanks. <strong>Danke schon</strong> = thanks a lot. <strong>Vielen Dank</strong> = many thanks (more formal).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Sorry",
      "h2": "Sorry & Excuse Me",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Entschuldigung</strong> works as 'excuse me' or 'sorry'. <strong>Es tut mir leid</strong> is a deeper 'I'm really sorry' — for bigger apologies.</p>"
